        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a815cf25-c935-5f0e-b516-903917563865",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lorde, Joel Little\n- Songs: \"Tennis Court\", \"Royals\", \"Mother Mother\", \"Heartlines\"\n- Albums and EPs: \"The Love Club EP\", \"Pure Heroine\"\n- Companies and Charts: Universal Music Group, Billboard Alternative Songs\n\nFacts:\n- In 2012, Lorde released \"Royals\" on her debut extended play \"The Love Club EP\".\n- On 7 June 2013, Universal Music Group released \"Tennis Court\" as the second single from \"Pure Heroine\", following \"Royals\".\n- In 2013, Lorde later included \"Royals\" on her debut studio album \"Pure Heroine\".\n- In August 2013, \"Royals\" by Lorde became the first song by a female solo artist to top the chart since \"Mother Mother\", by which time the chart had been renamed Billboard Alternative Songs.\n- Lorde and producer Joel Little co-wrote the song \"Heartlines\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b815f324-5996-5aa9-beb2-c5d39b5abdd6",
        "text": "Page: Tennis Court (song). Sentence: On 7 June 2013, the song was released as the album's second single by Universal Music Group, following \"Royals\".\nPage: Royals (song). Sentence: \"Royals\" is a song by New Zealand singer Lorde from her debut extended play album, \"The Love Club EP\" (2012).\nPage: Royals (song). Sentence: It was later included on her debut studio album, \"Pure Heroine\" (2013).\nPage: Mother Mother (song). Sentence: It was the last song by a female solo artist to top this chart until \"Royals\" by Lorde in August 2013, by which time the chart had been renamed \"Billboard\" Alternative Songs.\nPage: Heartlines. Sentence: The song was co-written by fellow New Zealand musician Lorde and the track's producer, Joel Little.",
